A||N||11||Haze_Performance||Need Trailer Hitch Help???||||10||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-25-2001||01:50 AM||||I have a trailer hitch that I want to slap on my 84 SE. What type & size hardware do I need to bolt it up? Please go easy on me.. I'm a virgin to the Fiero mounted hitch world..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Thank You<BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">     .     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">     .     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff_1.gif"> <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||09-25-2001||07:37 AM||||haze.  i just used 3/8 or 1/2 inch standard bolts.  about 1 1/2 or 2 inches long.  you will have to drill 4 small holes into the frame, but nothing major.  what i ended up doing was drilling the whole once i found the mark and putting the washer and bolt in thru the top.  then put the hitch up and fed the bolt thru the hitch.  and just put nuts on and was done.  i hope this helps.  <BR>email me if you have any questions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chester||09-25-2001||08:53 AM||||The hitch I got from the Fiero store lined up with 2 holes that were already on the frame.  Then I marked out the other two and drilled.  I don't remember the size of the bolts because they came with my hitch but I would recommend that you use high strength hardware to bolt it on (I think grade 8 or better?)<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ambush||09-25-2001||10:47 AM||||Why? You are putting this on a fiero right? What are you towing? a trailer alone should way as much as the fiero. To make things worse fiero brakes are not the best. Just think about it for a minute.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-25-2001||10:58 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ambush:<BR><B>Why? You are putting this on a fiero right? What are you towing? a trailer alone should way as much as the fiero. To make things worse fiero brakes are not the best. Just think about it for a minute.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trail02.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trail01.jpg">  <BR>These photos are of David Gageby's Fiero trailer. hidden under the front cover is a pair of Fiero seats with a center to mount an umbrella (matching of course) and an ashtray.<P><BR>Have you ever tried to take 2 people on a road trip to a Fiero show... with only your one Fiero?  My wife and I were PACKED into my GT for Fierorama!  I will someday find a dead Fiero to convert into a trailer to match my GT... weight certainly isn't much of an issue on this type of setup.  We're talking about a small carrier, not towing another car or a camper or something...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||09-25-2001||02:27 PM||||i towed a uhual trailer(4x8 @ 1200lbs give or take)  1100 miles from fla to NW indiana.  no problems at all.  im not sure of the exact weight of the trailer.  1200 is just a rough guess by what i had in it.  and that was with 150k miles on the clock.  not bad for a fiero.  i drove thru tennessee mountains and didnt have a problem.  the only slight problem i had was in Indiana. it was so windy i had to drive in 4th gear to keep it over 70mph. i have an 88 with the upgraded brakes so taht wasnt a problem at all.  and being an 88 could be the reason i had to drill all 4 wholes.  the hitch was from Outlaw performance and is a copy of fierostore's hitch.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jefrysuko||09-25-2001||02:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ambush:<BR><B>Why? You are putting this on a fiero right? What are you towing? a trailer alone should way as much as the fiero. To make things worse fiero brakes are not the best. Just think about it for a minute.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hase,<BR>Don't you just love unhelpful criticism?  Here is some more.  I think you should put it on the Indy so that it will lower the collector value of the car.  Better yet put it on the SC so that when you get that V8 in there you will have more available torque for towing.  Hey have you seen those trucks that have their hitch mounted in the bed?  Maybe you could just mount one of those to your decklid.  Sounds like fun to me.<P>BTW: I got my pictures developed from the Fierorama.  Do you want me to post the ones of you and the "Pink Lady?"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-25-2001||06:38 PM||||MinnGreenGT--If the rear window is still in place (on the trailer), wouldn't that put alot of drag on both the trailer and the car?  (We could have used one of those at Fierorama, huh?)||||reg||1
